"span":{"data":{"file_id":3,"beg":{"line":664,"col":5},"end":{"line":664,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":74,"kind":{"StorageDead":2},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"data":{"file_id":3,"beg":{"line":664,"col":5},"end":{"line":664,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":75,"kind":{"StorageDead":1},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"data":{"file_id":3,"beg":{"line":664,"col":5},"end":{"line":664,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":76,"kind":"Return","comments_before":[]}]},"comments":[]}}}],"global_decls":[null,null],"trait_decls":[{"def_id":0,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["convert",0]},{"Ident":["AsRef",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":5,"beg":{"line":219,"col":0},"end":{"line":219,"col":52}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Used to do a cheap reference-to-reference conversion."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This trait is similar to [`AsMut`] which is used for converting between mutable references."},{"DocComment":" If you need to do a costly conversion it is better to implement [`From`] with type"},{"DocComment":" `&T` or write a custom function."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Relation to `Borrow`"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `AsRef` has the same signature as [`Borrow`], but [`Borrow`] is different in a few aspects:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" - Unlike `AsRef`, [`Borrow`] has a blanket impl for any `T`, and can be used to accept either"},{"DocComment":"   a reference or a value. (See also note on `AsRef`'s reflexibility below.)"},{"DocComment":" - [`Borrow`] also requires that [`Hash`], [`Eq`] and [`Ord`] for a borrowed value are"},{"DocComment":"   equivalent to those of the owned value. For this reason, if you want to"},{"DocComment":"   borrow only a single field of a struct you can implement `AsRef`, but not [`Borrow`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" **Note: This trait must not fail**. If the conversion can fail, use a"},{"DocComment":" dedicated method which returns an [`Option<T>`] or a [`Result<T, E>`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Generic Implementations"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `AsRef` auto-dereferences if the inner type is a reference or a mutable reference"},{"DocComment":" (e.g.: `foo.as_ref()` will work the same if `foo` has type `&mut Foo` or `&&mut Foo`)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that due to historic reasons, the above currently does not hold generally for all"},{"DocComment":" [dereferenceable types], e.g. `foo.as_ref()` will *not* work the same as"},{"DocComment":" `Box::new(foo).as_ref()`. Instead, many smart pointers provide an `as_ref` implementation which"},{"DocComment":" simply returns a reference to the [pointed-to value] (but do not perform a cheap"},{"DocComment":" reference-to-reference conversion for that value). However, [`AsRef::as_ref`] should not be"},{"DocComment":" used for the sole purpose of dereferencing; instead ['`Deref` coercion'] can be used:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [dereferenceable types]: core::ops::Deref"},{"DocComment":" [pointed-to value]: core::ops::Deref::Target"},{"DocComment":" ['`Deref` coercion']: core::ops::Deref#deref-coercion"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let x = Box::new(5i32);"},{"DocComment":" // Avoid this:"},{"DocComment":" // let y: &i32 = x.as_ref();"},{"DocComment":" // Better just write:"},{"DocComment":" let y: &i32 = &x;"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Types which implement [`Deref`] should consider implementing `AsRef<T>` as follows:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`Deref`]: core::ops::Deref"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" # use core::ops::Deref;"},{"DocComment":" # struct SomeType;"},{"DocComment":" # impl Deref for SomeType {"},{"DocComment":" #     type Target = [u8];"},{"DocComment":" #     fn deref(&self) -> &[u8] {"},{"DocComment":" #         &[]"},{"DocComment":" #     }"},{"DocComment":" # }"},{"DocComment":" impl<T> AsRef<T> for SomeType"},{"DocComment":" where"},{"DocComment":"     T: ?Sized,"},{"DocComment":"     <SomeType as Deref>::Target: AsRef<T>,"},{"DocComment":" {"},{"DocComment":"     fn as_ref(&self) -> &T {"},{"DocComment":"         self.deref().as_ref()"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Reflexivity"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Ideally, `AsRef` would be reflexive, i.e. there would be an `impl<T: ?Sized> AsRef<T> for T`"},{"DocComment":" with [`as_ref`] simply returning its argument unchanged."},{"DocComment":" Such a blanket implementation is currently *not* provided due to technical restrictions of"},{"DocComment":" Rust's type system (it would be overlapping with another existing blanket implementation for"},{"DocComment":" `&T where T: AsRef<U>` which allows `AsRef` to auto-dereference, see \"Generic Implementations\""},{"DocComment":" above)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`as_ref`]: AsRef::as_ref"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" A trivial implementation of `AsRef<T> for T` must be added explicitly for a particular type `T`"},{"DocComment":" where needed or desired. Note, however, that not all types from `std` contain such an"},{"DocComment":" implementation, and those cannot be added by external code due to orphan rules."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" By using trait bounds we can accept arguments of different types as long as they can be"},{"DocComment":" converted to the specified type `T`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For example: By creating a generic function that takes an `AsRef<str>` we express that we"},{"DocComment":" want to accept all references that can be converted to [`&str`] as an argument."},{"DocComment":" Since both [`String`] and [`&str`] implement `AsRef<str>` we can accept both as input argument."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`&str`]: primitive@str"},{"DocComment":" [`Borrow`]: crate::borrow::Borrow"},{"DocComment":" [`Eq`]: crate::cmp::Eq"},{"DocComment":" [`Ord`]: crate::cmp::Ord"},{"DocComment":" [`String`]: ../../std/string/struct.String.html"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" fn is_hello<T: AsRef<str>>(s: T) {"},{"DocComment":"    assert_eq!(\"hello\", s.as_ref());"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let s = \"hello\";"},{"DocComment":" is_hello(s);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let s = \"hello\".to_string();"},{"DocComment":" is_hello(s);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"AsRef"},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"T"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[],"consts":[],"types":[],"methods":[{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"as_ref","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["convert",0]},{"Ident":["AsRef",0]},{"Ident":["as_ref",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":5,"beg":{"line":222,"col":4},"end":{"line":222,"col":27}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Converts this type into a shared reference of the (usually inferred) input type."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"HashConsedValue":[1001,{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"HashConsedValue":[1000,{"TypeVar":{"Free":0}}]},"Shared"]}]}],"output":{"HashConsedValue":[1003,{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"HashConsedValue":[1002,{"TypeVar":{"Free":1}}]},"Shared"]}]}},"default":null},"kind":{"TraitMethod":[0,0]}}],"vtable":{"id":{"Adt":6},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":1002}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}},{"def_id":1,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["ops",0]},{"Ident":["index",0]},{"Ident":["Index",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":12,"beg":{"line":59,"col":0},"end":{"line":59,"col":34}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Used for indexing operations (`container[index]`) in immutable contexts."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `container[index]` is actually syntactic sugar for `*container.index(index)`,"},{"DocComment":" but only when used as an immutable value. If a mutable value is requested,"},{"DocComment":" [`IndexMut`] is used instead. This allows nice things such as"},{"DocComment":" `let value = v[index]` if the type of `value` implements [`Copy`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The following example implements `Index` on a read-only `NucleotideCount`"},{"DocComment":" container, enabling individual counts to be retrieved with index syntax."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::ops::Index;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" enum Nucleotide {"},{"DocComment":"     A,"},{"DocComment":"     C,"},{"DocComment":"     G,"},{"DocComment":"     T,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" struct NucleotideCount {"},{"DocComment":"     a: usize,"},{"DocComment":"     c: usize,"},{"DocComment":"     g: usize,"},{"DocComment":"     t: usize,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" impl Index<Nucleotide> for NucleotideCount {"},{"DocComment":"     type Output = usize;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":"     fn index(&self, nucleotide: Nucleotide) -> &Self::Output {"},{"DocComment":"         match nucleotide {"},{"DocComment":"             Nucleotide::A => &self.a,"},{"DocComment":"             Nucleotide::C => &self.c,"},{"DocComment":"             Nucleotide::G => &self.g,"},{"DocComment":"             Nucleotide::T => &self.t,"},{"DocComment":"         }"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let nucleotide_count = NucleotideCount {a: 14, c: 9, g: 10, t: 12};"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(nucleotide_count[Nucleotide::A], 14);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(nucleotide_count[Nucleotide::C], 9);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(nucleotide_count[Nucleotide::G], 10);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(nucleotide_count[Nucleotide::T], 12);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"index"},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"Idx"},{"index":2,"name":"Self_Output"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"implied_clauses":[],"consts":[],"types":[null],"methods":[{"params":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"name":"index","item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["ops",0]},{"Ident":["index",0]},{"Ident":["Index",0]},{"Ident":["index",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":12,"beg":{"line":73,"col":4},"end":{"line":73,"col":49}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Performs the indexing (`container[index]`) operation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" May panic if the index is out of bounds."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":1001},{"Deduplicated":1002}],"output":{"HashConsedValue":[1005,{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Bound":[0,0]}},{"HashConsedValue":[1004,{"TypeVar":{"Free":2}}]},"Shared"]}]}},"default":null},"kind":{"TraitMethod":[1,0]}}],"vtable":{"id":{"Adt":14},"g